# Laptop screen tool — where new features go

This is the safe place to work: pages, weather, notifications, images,
autostart, pacing. Use `.venv/bin/python`.

## What the screen can draw (fixed by firmware — do not assume more)
- 240x240 panel, RGB565 colours via `sp.rgb()` / `sp.hexcolor()`. x right, y down.
- `fill`, `text` (8x16 ASCII font, chars 32..126 only, `scale` 1..8, always draws its
  background), `image` (RGB565, must fit on screen), `mono` (1-bit bitmap).
- No fonts other than the built-in one, no transparency, no scrolling, no reading back.
- Bandwidth is low (~1 KB/s, about 60 ms per packet). Full-screen RGB images take
  minutes: keep images small (icons <= 64x64) or use `mono`.

## Widget and page conventions (`rt100screen.py`)
- A page is `fn(now, data) -> dict[key, Widget]`; register it in `PAGES` with its data source.
- `Screen` redraws only widgets whose value changed, so keep widget values stable
  (round numbers, fixed-width `Text.chars`) to avoid sending every second.
- Text is padded to `chars` so old text is overwritten; pass non-ASCII through `ascii_only`.
- Keep the page dots at y=224 free; leave a 16 px margin at the sides.
- Data sources must never raise or block more than ~1 s (use timeouts, return None on failure).
- No new pip dependencies without asking; prefer stdlib, `psutil`, `busctl --json`.

## Testing order
1. `.venv/bin/python rt100screen.py <action> --dry-run` — inspect packets.
2. If you changed `clock_page`/`system_page`/`media_page` signatures, update
   `re/custom/emu_custom.py`, then run it and look at `re/custom/out/emu_*.png`.
3. Only then send to the device (check `pgrep -af rt100screen` first) and ask the user
   what the screen shows — you cannot see it.

## Do not
- Do not edit `Link._session` framing (0x31 count in bytes 1-2, checksum at byte 7,
  no-op padding in `finally`) or remove the pacing sleeps.
- Do not send packets outside `Link.send`.
- Autostart (systemd user unit) must run `rt100screen.py run` only, restart on
  failure with a delay of at least 5 s, and the user must approve enabling it.
